-- =========================================================================
-- Expr + Pattern — the irreducible core expression ADT and its pattern
-- sub-ADT. expr-substrate Phase 1 (brief:
-- `workstreams/expr-substrate/briefs/phase-1-register-syntax-expr.md`).
--
-- `Expr` is the locked 7-case core: the surface sugars (`if` / `let` / `do`
-- / infix operators) are NOT cases — they are calls / applied-lambdas /
-- sequences, lowered into these seven by `desugar` (Phase 2). It is the
-- successor to the engine-side `CoreExpr` (`fenel/modules/engine/ir-ast.fenel`,
-- 10 cases): `CoreExpr` minus `{CoreIf, CoreLet, CoreDo}` = exactly these
-- seven (verified, Phase-0 audit Task 2). The `CoreExpr → Expr` registry
-- replace is staged behind this registration (its own brief — see the
-- roadmap completion note on the Step-2 NO-GO).
--
-- TYPING DISCIPLINE (brief decision 5): this mirrors `CoreExpr`'s live,
-- registration-proven discipline byte-for-byte — precise `String` where the
-- locked block names it (`name` / `fnId` / `ctor`), and the loose untracked
-- `a` for every recursive / payload slot (`value` / `args` / `body` / `arms`
-- / `fields` / `params` / `scrutinee`). The locked block's precise
-- self-referential / tuple forms (`args: List Expr`, `arms: List (Pattern,
-- Expr)`, `fields: List (String, Expr)`) are a later-phase precision upgrade,
-- NOT P1's — the Step-0 probe confirmed loose `a` parses + registers cleanly
-- and keeps the eventual `CoreExpr`-replace shape-identical (the byte-equality
-- lever). `a` is a free type variable (no head param), exactly as `CoreExpr`
-- declares it.
--
-- DELTA (brief decision 2 + Phase-0 delta #1): `EConstruct` carries the
-- `fields` slot (`ctor: String args: a fields: a`), mirroring
-- `CoreConstruct.fields` — the Phase-21.1 named-field metadata. Dropping it
-- regresses the named-field self-host path (the `ir-ast.fenel` header
-- documents the exact historical bug). Same for `PatConstruct.fields`.
--
-- OQ3 = (a) (brief decision 1): `Pattern` is registered alongside `Expr` in
-- this same file. Its 4 cases are `CorePattern`'s (PatLit / PatVar /
-- PatWildcard / PatConstruct) — the Pat* names are kept (they don't collide
-- with the Core* prefix sweep). No `guard` PATTERN case: guards LANDED
-- (fenel-surface-extensions Phase 3) as an arm-level field on the SMatch/EMatch
-- arm record (`{pattern, guard, body}`, D1 option A — a guard is an arm
-- condition, not a pattern), so the 4 Pattern cases stay structural. The
-- lowering uses a transient `PatGuard` MARSHAL marker (syntaxToJsonLogic ⇒ the
-- ledgered `$guard` `$`-key marshal); it is NOT a registered Pattern case.
-- desugar PRESERVES the arm `guard` field, but the compile passes do not yet
-- consume it (the compiled-guard fence — interpreter-only today).
--
-- Registered codeName = `Expr` / `Pattern` (decl name = codeName); the
-- canonical long codeName (`Expression`) is Phase 10's to formalise (it owns
-- the short-codeName typeclass). Authored via the Ext-1 entity-facet path
-- (`@label`/`@description` directives → lifted Codeable → auto-register in
-- `system-entities.ts`), threaded through `type-foundation.ts`'s load pass.
-- =========================================================================

@entity
@label "Expression"
@description "The irreducible core expression — the 7-case ADT every Fenel function body reduces to. Surface sugars (if / let / do / infix) are NOT cases: `if` is `ECall \"if\"`, `let` is an applied `ELambda`, `do` is a sequence, operators are calls via Infixable. Successor to the engine-side CoreExpr (CoreExpr minus If/Let/Do). EConstruct carries the named-field `fields` slot (Phase-21.1 metadata)."
Expr a =
  ELit value: a
  | EVar name: String
  | ECall fnId: String args: a
  | ELambda params: a body: a
  | EMatch scrutinee: a arms: a
  | EConstruct ctor: String args: a fields: a
  | ERecord fields: a

@entity
@label "Pattern"
@description "A match pattern — the sub-ADT EMatch arms bind against. 4 cases mirroring the engine-side CorePattern: PatLit (literal) / PatVar (binding) / PatWildcard / PatConstruct (constructor, carrying the Phase-21.1 named-field `fields` metadata). No guard case yet — guards (TODO 89-90) are an anticipated FUTURE additive case, not a dead slot today."
Pattern a =
  PatLit value: a
  | PatVar name: String
  | PatWildcard
  | PatConstruct ctor: String args: a fields: a
